/OBJ
;obj  starts  weight    c w  5 4 3 2 1 0 9 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 1 0    noun   adjective
/0    0           1     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    BENCH  _
/1    0           1     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    KEY    _
/2    0           5     _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _    CHEST  _

/PRO 0
; Entry 1: carry-through proof. Flags 100/101 and object 1's CARRIED
; location all arrived from part A verbatim - all 256 flags copy across
; a switch, and object locations copy by index for as many objects as
; both parts define in common (see authoring-kit\SETUP.md's multi-part
; "Author caveats" for the full rules a real game must follow).
> _ _   EQ 100 77
        EQ 101 88
        CARRIED 1
        MES "PB CARRY OK#n"
        SKIP 1
> _ _   MES "PB CARRY F#n"

; Entry 2: PARTn asset probe proof. Part A's own 0.XMB is staged at the
; SD root (sd\0.XMB); part B's is staged separately at sd\PART2\0.XMB,
; with DIFFERENT bytes at the same internal offset. XMES only prints
; this clean sentence if ext_xmes's PARTn\ probe (SP11 Task 5) actually
; won the race against the root file - a probe that wrongly fell
; through to the root 0.XMB would read A's bytes at B's offset instead,
; producing garbled or simply wrong text, not a crash and not silence.
> _ _   XMES "part two external text via PART2"
        NEWLINE

; Entry 3: same-part SAVE/LOAD round trip while curPart = 2 - the first
; place in the whole test corpus that exercises h_save/h_load away from
; curPart = 1 (condacts.dsf's own SAVE/LOAD checks always run at part
; 1). Type any 1-8 character name, then the SAME name again at the
; second prompt. SAVE/LOAD are condition-typed here: either failing
; aborts this entry immediately and falls to "PB SAV F" below, the same
; idiom condacts.dsf check 62 uses for its own round trip.
> _ _   MES "PB TYPE NAME: p2#n"
        LET 110 55
        SAVE 0
        LET 110 0
        MES "PB TYPE NAME: p2#n"
        LOAD 0
        EQ 110 55
        MES "PB SAV OK#n"
        SKIP 1
> _ _   MES "PB SAV F#n"

; Entry 4: the return leg, mirroring part A's own outbound switch
; (NDPARTA.DSF entry 1) - fail-silent on a missing GAME.DDB, same idiom
; as condacts.dsf check 44. On success this entry never finishes.
> _ _   EXTERN 1 4
        MES "PB SWITCH F#n"
/END
